-- PROGRAM -------------------- errors/cap_needs_10.march

`file_write` is internal to the standard library; use `File.write`. [stdlib_internal]

14 |     let _ = file_write("/tmp/n", int_to_string(n))
                 ^^^^^^^^^^


    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

14 -     let _ = file_write("/tmp/n", int_to_string(n))
14 +     let _ = Authority.must(File.write("/tmp/n", int_to_string(n)))


-- CAPABILITY ----------------- errors/cap_needs_10.march

`save` writes a file, but module `Main` declares no `needs IO.FileWrite`, and `main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)`. [cap_needs]
hint: add this to the module body —
        needs IO.FileWrite
and give `main` a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` parameter: `fn main(…, _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite))`.

14 |     let _ = file_write("/tmp/n", int_to_string(n))
                 ^^^^^^^^^^


    `main` calls `save` here:

19 |     save(1)
         ^^^^

    `main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here:

18 |   fn main(c : Cap(IO.Console)) do
              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

10 | mod Main do
11 +   needs IO.FileWrite
18 -   fn main(c : Cap(IO.Console)) do
18 +   fn main(c : Cap(IO.Console), _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite)) do

